2026-11-18 Flutter chat jump button and send-position validation

Baseline with the corrected test fixture: sending moved the visible history message by 469.98 logical pixels on Android and 449.17 on iOS. The jump button was absent on both.
The first send-position fix exposed a separate 86 logical pixel shift when clearing a multiline composer. The final fix compensates for the viewport height change during that send layout.
Final: all 97 Flutter chat and chat-sheet widget tests passed (reporter elapsed time about 7 seconds). The tests cover a stable visible history message during multiline send and answer growth, and a jump button that appears away from the bottom and returns to the latest message both during and after generation.
Targeted Dart analysis reported no errors or warnings. Two existing Flutter Material import deprecation notices remain.
Validation used local widget fixtures and a fake streaming repository. No live API calls, model tokens, or API costs. Device latency was not measured.
